WEBVTT

1
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.205
With any investment, comes risk.

2
00:00:23.205 --> 00:00:26.175
Investing in the futures
market is no exception.

3
00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:28.425
That's just the nature
of the investing world.

4
00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:31.470
Since futures are
derivatives, like options,

5
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.135
they can derive their value from

6
00:00:33.135 --> 00:00:35.340
other underlying
financial instruments,

7
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.840
such as equities, bonds,

8
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.400
or currencies, each with
their own inherent risks.

9
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.320
You should keep in
mind that risks

10
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.850
come in different forms.

11
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.230
For example, as an investor,

12
00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:46.880
you're typically face scenarios

13
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.650
where you buy
something that loses

14
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:52.520
value or something you
sell rises in value.

15
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.170
Such risks may be due to

16
00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.120
an adverse move in
the market itself,

17
00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.920
or may have been
that you decided to

18
00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.720
enter the market at a poor time,

19
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:03.935
which in finance is generally
referred to as market risk.

20
00:01:03.935 --> 00:01:06.680
Alternatively, you may
have purchased a stock

21
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.100
that perform badly when
the broader market sold,

22
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:14.005
which is typically a signal
of company-specific risk.

23
00:01:14.005 --> 00:01:16.160
You can probably
find a case each day

24
00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.080
of the week where
the market rises,

25
00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.195
but some stocks fall.

26
00:01:20.195 --> 00:01:22.040
Generally investors invest in

27
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.300
stocks because they believe that

28
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.270
the value of company's tends
to increase over time.

29
00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.400
As good economic policy creates

30
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.190
an increasingly
improving labor market,

31
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.200
you could say that
the futures market

32
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.030
differs in this respect as

33
00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.350
buyers and sellers tend to have

34
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:39.050
more balanced view due
to competing bullish,

35
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:42.100
bearish information
on most commodities.

36
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.260
However the futures markets
by their very nature,

37
00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:48.020
perform another very important
role when it comes to

38
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.110
mitigating risk as
the futures exchange,

39
00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.930
where standardized futures
contracts are traded,

40
00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:56.550
bears the role of
central counter-party

41
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.720
to all transactions.

42
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.440
Futures trading, like

43
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.585
any other typical
financial transaction,

44
00:02:02.585 --> 00:02:04.610
generally involves two parties,

45
00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.520
a willing buyer and
a willing seller.

46
00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.370
The role of a
marketplace is to bring

47
00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:14.075
counter-parties together and
engage in price discovery.

48
00:02:14.075 --> 00:02:15.920
This process between a bank and

49
00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.750
its customer is often referred

50
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.650
to as over the counter
or OTC trading.

51
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.320
However, the relationship
among buyers and sellers in

52
00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.820
the market place raises

53
00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.085
the question of
counter-party risk,

54
00:02:28.085 --> 00:02:30.410
since neither party can guarantee

55
00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:33.250
that the other will
not fail on the trade.

56
00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.690
The purpose of an
exchange facility or

57
00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:37.940
transactional model is to remove

58
00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.800
counter-party risk
by creating and

59
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.070
transferring risk to the
single exchange entity,

60
00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.880
backed by the diverse financial
standing of its members.

61
00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.790
Sure, there are buyers and
sellers to all transactions,

62
00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.130
but the exchange
undertakes to back

63
00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.350
all futures contracts regardless

64
00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:56.810
of the financial health
of anyone trading on it.

65
00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.850
This alleviate settlement risk,

66
00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.460
meaning participants in the
market don't need to check

67
00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.085
the quality or capitalization

68
00:03:04.085 --> 00:03:06.590
of the person or company
they're trading with.

69
00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.415
This is all done by the exchange.

70
00:03:09.415 --> 00:03:11.840
To further help safeguard
the futures market,

71
00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.850
the Commodity Futures
Trading Commission,

72
00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:17.030
or CFTC, it was
established by Congress

73
00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.650
in the mid 1970s to serve
as a federal regulator.

74
00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.960
This capacity, the CFTC acts
to ensure the integrity of

75
00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.075
futures market pricing with

76
00:03:26.075 --> 00:03:28.745
aims to prevent abusive
trading practices,

77
00:03:28.745 --> 00:03:31.430
fraud, as well as the
regulation of brokers

78
00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:34.885
that participate in futures
trading activities.

79
00:03:34.885 --> 00:03:37.010
Now that we've touched
on and explored

80
00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:39.160
different types of risks
in the financial markets,

81
00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.580
we'll next turn our attention to

82
00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.590
futures prices with a focus

83
00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:46.505
on the difference between
spot and forward prices.

84
00:03:46.505 --> 00:03:49.050
We'll look forward to
you joining us then.